@startuml
!include style.puml
title Stewart in context

actor "PHP developer" as dev

rectangle "Home Assistant" as ha $ha {
    component "WebSocket API\n/api/websocket" as ws
    component "Entity registry\n& state machine" as reg
}

rectangle "Stewart daemon" as stewart $broker {
    component "Broker" as broker
    component "Workers" as workers
}

rectangle "Your repository" as repo $usercode {
    component "apps/*.php\nautomations" as apps
    component "stewart.yaml\n.env" as cfg
}

dev --> apps : writes ordinary\nPHP classes
dev --> cfg : registers apps,\nsupplies token

apps ..> workers : loaded and run by
cfg ..> broker : configures

broker <-> ws : one authenticated\nWebSocket connection
ws -- reg

note bottom of stewart
  Runs on a **separate host** from Home Assistant,
  so it authenticates with a long-lived token over
  the network. There is no Supervisor add-on path.
end note
@enduml
